{"authored" [{"question" "q-18279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/state.json" "file_sha256" "05786aea1e56ef3aef192ce1e255c6e92b272cb439bf841a65b500c7b7e3df41" "basis" 1483 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+4|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(6-0)+2(0+1)+4(0+3) \\\\  & =6+2+12 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-4-0) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21}=\\frac{1}{20}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/state.json" "file_sha256" "05786aea1e56ef3aef192ce1e255c6e92b272cb439bf841a65b500c7b7e3df41" "basis" 1483 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "992dea1d37f7b1550b3a49acce88204d708ff8d6bc4b0fdc6f634b06cf9cc40b" "basis" 1483 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/state.json" "file_sha256" "05786aea1e56ef3aef192ce1e255c6e92b272cb439bf841a65b500c7b7e3df41" "basis" 1483 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/state.json" "file_sha256" "05786aea1e56ef3aef192ce1e255c6e92b272cb439bf841a65b500c7b7e3df41" "basis" 1483 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/state.json" "file_sha256" "05786aea1e56ef3aef192ce1e255c6e92b272cb439bf841a65b500c7b7e3df41" "basis" 1483 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/state.json" "file_sha256" "05786aea1e56ef3aef192ce1e255c6e92b272cb439bf841a65b500c7b7e3df41" "basis" 1483 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{20}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/state.json" "file_sha256" "05786aea1e56ef3aef192ce1e255c6e92b272cb439bf841a65b500c7b7e3df41" "basis" 1483 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/state.json" "file_sha256" "05786aea1e56ef3aef192ce1e255c6e92b272cb439bf841a65b500c7b7e3df41" "basis" 1483 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ k & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nequals $-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/state.json" "file_sha256" "05786aea1e56ef3aef192ce1e255c6e92b272cb439bf841a65b500c7b7e3df41" "basis" 1483 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ k & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ k & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ k & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\,(1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1))-2\\,(0\\cdot 2-1\\cdot k)+(-1)\\,(0\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot k) \\\\  & =(2+1)-2\\,(-k)+(-1)\\,(-k) \\\\  & =3+2k+k \\\\  & =3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-(4-1) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3k+3}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{3k+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2}$, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-3}{3k+3} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -3k-3 & =-6 \\\\ -3k & =-6+3 \\\\ k & =\\frac{-3}{-3} \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/state.json" "file_sha256" "05786aea1e56ef3aef192ce1e255c6e92b272cb439bf841a65b500c7b7e3df41" "basis" 1483 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "992dea1d37f7b1550b3a49acce88204d708ff8d6bc4b0fdc6f634b06cf9cc40b" "basis" 1483 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319859" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/state.json" "file_sha256" "05786aea1e56ef3aef192ce1e255c6e92b272cb439bf841a65b500c7b7e3df41" "basis" 1483 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040679/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-18279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-18279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+4|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(6-0)+2(0+1)+4(0+3) \\\\  & =6+2+12 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-4-0) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21}=\\frac{1}{20}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-18279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d14a6f5198acbc6ec79e8ddfa7ff207290ba8cb1557c6280b4f983b58bb65b49"} {"question" "q-18279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-18279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{20}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-18279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-104416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-104416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}A=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =(-1)|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2+1)-(1-2)+0 \\\\  & =-3+1+0 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{13} & =(-1)^{1+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1-4 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{31}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}=\\frac{1}{-2}\\cdot (-5)=\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-104416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d14a6f5198acbc6ec79e8ddfa7ff207290ba8cb1557c6280b4f983b58bb65b49"} {"question" "q-104416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-104416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{5}"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-104416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-104439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The entry ${a}_{22}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & k & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $-\\frac{1}{4}$ and $det(A)=k-4.$ Find the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-104439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=k-4\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{22}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{22}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{22} & =(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{22}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{22} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-4}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{22}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{4}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{1}{k-4} \\\\ k-4 & =-4 \\\\ k & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-104439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d14a6f5198acbc6ec79e8ddfa7ff207290ba8cb1557c6280b4f983b58bb65b49"} {"question" "q-104439" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-104439" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-104439" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-319420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n${a}_{31}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-319420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\,(2+1)-0\\,(0-1)+2\\,(-0-2) \\\\  & =3-0-4 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}^{t}={c}_{13}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{13} & =(-1)^{1+3}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-0 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{31}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-319420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d14a6f5198acbc6ec79e8ddfa7ff207290ba8cb1557c6280b4f983b58bb65b49"} {"question" "q-319420" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-319420" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-319859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ k & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nequals $-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-319859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ k & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ k & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ k & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\,(1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1))-2\\,(0\\cdot 2-1\\cdot k)+(-1)\\,(0\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot k) \\\\  & =(2+1)-2\\,(-k)+(-1)\\,(-k) \\\\  & =3+2k+k \\\\  & =3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-(4-1) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3k+3}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{3k+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2}$, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-3}{3k+3} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -3k-3 & =-6 \\\\ -3k & =-6+3 \\\\ k & =\\frac{-3}{-3} \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-319859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d14a6f5198acbc6ec79e8ddfa7ff207290ba8cb1557c6280b4f983b58bb65b49"} {"question" "q-319859" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"} {"question" "q-319859" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064278/state.json" "file_sha256" "000aa930a10547ee4a5223f27b4f67fd197fdc6075c13b816f7f6f1bffe7e76d"}] "usage" {"q-18279" [] "q-319859" []} "basis" 2098 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186057207 17592186057208 17592186057209 17592186